On Thu, Jul 3, 2008 at 6:15 PM, namor <eldrikdo@gmail.com> wrote:
>>
>> {za'a roroiku le prenu cu gelki gi'anai citka}
>> "I observe that, on each occasion, it is true that the person is happy
>> if it is true that the person eats"
>
> Would {za'a roroiku le prenu cu gelki ijanai ri citka} mean the same?
> What exactly does {roroiku} bind to, how does it work with multiple bridi?
> (priority question)

{roroiku} is a term, it will only belong to the first bridi in that case, so
it won't be equivalent. But these would be:

{za'a roroiku ga le prenu cu gleki ginai ri citka}
{za'a roroiku zo'u le prenu cu gelki .ijanai ri citka}

mu'o mi'e xorxes


